{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"prompt\": \"Use case: stylized-concept. Create a landscape 3:2 Minecraft builder reference sheet, crisp vanilla Minecraft voxel blocks only, plain light ivory background, no characters or animals. Two views side by side, LEFT straight-on orthographic front elevation, RIGHT three-quarter view of the identical build at the same block scale. Entire buildings and ground visible. Skilled human builder quality with real massing, proud piers, recessed framed openings, stairs/slabs/fences/walls/trapdoors/lantern detail, actual roof verges, eaves and ridges.\\nSite: Victorian high-street terrace of exactly three attached red-brick shop-houses on cobblestone and andesite street with pale polished_andesite pavement. Each house exactly 13 blocks wide, total 39 wide; lot 33 deep, buildings 18 deep. Tall shop storey plus two storeys of flats plus gable loft, ridge y25. Each house has its own steep 45-degree grey-slate front gable, three matching sawtooth gables meeting in valleys at party walls. Cream sandstone piers stand one block proud dividing houses and rise to strong sandstone cornices under gables. Sandstone coping edges verges. Wide open shopfront per house under dark-oak fascia: left bookseller blue awning and exact lettering \\\"BOOKS\\\"; middle florist green and pink awning and \\\"FLORA\\\"; right ironmonger red awning and \\\"TOOLS\\\". Use stepped stair and banner awnings. Spruce counters and glass fins behind open fronts. Each fascia has a hanging sign on bracket and lantern beneath awning. Narrow brick bay beside EACH shop holds dark-oak residents' front door, glass fanlight, lantern on each side. Above sandstone string course, each house has THREE recessed window groups per flat floor, centre group triple-width; centre first-floor window has small iron Juliet balcony. Sandstone sills/lintels, grey stone-brick base. One attic window per front gable. Rear brick chimney per house climbs above rear ridge, stone band, slab cap, white campfire smoke. Small brick-walled rear yards with grass and paths, visible as much as camera permits.\\nExact block palette by role (use these Minecraft ids; needed stair/slab variants of these materials are allowed; spruce counter components are allowed as specified):\\nWALLS: bricks, brick_stairs, brick_slab, brick_wall.\\nTRIM: smooth_sandstone, smooth_sandstone_stairs, smooth_sandstone_slab, cut_sandstone, sandstone_wall.\\nFASCIA: dark_oak_planks, dark_oak_stairs, dark_oak_slab, dark_oak_door, dark_oak_fence, dark_oak_trapdoor, dark_oak_hanging_sign.\\nROOF: cobbled_deepslate, deepslate_tiles, polished_deepslate, polished_blackstone_bricks, stone_bricks, with appropriate stairs/slabs for steep roofs.\\nBASE: stone_bricks, stone_brick_stairs, stone_brick_slab.\\nPAVING: polished_andesite.\\nROAD: cobblestone, andesite.\\nGLASS: glass_pane.\\nSHOP: dark_prismarine_stairs, waxed_oxidized_cut_copper_stairs, red_nether_brick_stairs, quartz_stairs, blue_wall_banner, green_wall_banner, red_wall_banner, white_wall_banner.\\nPRODUCT: bookshelf, flower_pot, potted_azalea_bush, potted_pink_tulip, anvil, barrel.\\nGROUND: stone.\\nYARD: grass_block, coarse_dirt, dirt_path.\\nFunctional/decor: iron_bars, lantern, iron_chain, ladder, hay_block, campfire. Spruce counters: spruce_planks, spruce_stairs, spruce_slab, spruce_trapdoor.\\nNo invented non-Minecraft materials, no smooth realistic geometry. Preserve block grid and restrained Victorian detail. The two views are the focus; no palette swatches or extensive labels needed.\",\n  \"roles\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"WALLS\",\n      \"blocks\": [\"bricks\", \"brick_stairs\", \"brick_slab\", \"brick_wall\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"TRIM\",\n      \"blocks\": [\"smooth_sandstone\", \"smooth_sandstone_stairs\", \"smooth_sandstone_slab\", \"cut_sandstone\", \"sandstone_wall\", \"sandstone\", \"sandstone_stairs\", \"sandstone_slab\", \"cut_sandstone_slab\"]\n    },\n